note irequiv fixture (issue 826): rotate a byte right, traps included.
note r8 is copied verbatim from seed/omc/om2/s1/rot.om line 21 (omega-mv 62d1d0d6);
note for n >= 8 its shr traps 7 (amount at or above the width).
note r8w is a refactor through a doubled ushort, keeping that trap explicitly.
note r8m is a deliberate mutant that masks n with 7: same values for n < 8, but
note a value instead of trap 7 for every n >= 8.
fn r8 x uchar n uchar to uchar
if eq n 0
ret x
end
ret or shr x n shl x sub 8 n
end
fn r8w x uchar n uchar to uchar
if ge n 8
trap 7
end
d = or shl ushort x 8 ushort x
e = and shr d ushort n 255
ret uchar e
end
fn r8m x uchar n uchar to uchar
k = and n 7
if eq k 0
ret x
end
ret or shr x k shl x sub 8 k
end
